╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  Purpose
    Measure the per-stage cost of the governance layer — the Runtime-Context plane, the Replay
    plane, and the full pipeline — plus per-stage latency distributions from the recorded agent
    traces, to quantify overhead.

  Scientific motivation
    A guard nobody can afford to deploy is not a guard. Attributing cost to specific planes shows
    which parts of the architecture dominate, and whether the overhead is in the decision itself
    or in the evidence machinery around it.

  Why this experiment exists
    Turns 'overhead is low' into a per-stage number a systems reviewer can audit.

