  Scientific meaning, per family (verbatim from the executed artifact)
    missing_predicate  [A]
      A required node predicate is unavailable (missing key -> False).
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    delayed_predicate  [A]
      A predicate has not returned before the freshness window closes.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    corrupted_predicate  [A]
      A predicate carries an out-of-domain / adversarial value.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    conflicting_predicate  [A]
      Node-level and class-level signals disagree (both directions).
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    stale_context  [A]
      The runtime context is stale / telemetry not fresh.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    missing_authorization_context  [A]
      No valid permit token / authority signature is present.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    authorization_timeout  [A]
      A predicate evaluation times out; harness presents it as unavailable.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    network_delay  [A]
      Network delay -> telemetry not fresh and context stale.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    partial_system_failure  [A]
      A subset of predicate services is down.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    predicate_race_condition  [A]
      Concurrent predicate evaluations disagree; fail-closed resolution.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    clock_skew  [C]
      Clock skew beyond the freshness bound manifests as stale telemetry/context.
      Required property: fault -> SAFE_STATE and unauthorized flag set; 0 false permits
      Recovery: engine returns SAFE_STATE; execution interlock withholds actuation until a fresh
      clean proposal is presented (fail-closed, no auto-permit).
    replay_corruption  [B]
      A recorded hash_current is tampered.
      Required property: clean slice PASSES; mutated slice DETECTED (verifier exits non-zero)
      Recovery: verifier flags the break; the append-only chain is not advanced past the
      corrupted record (no downstream actuation on a broken chain).
    ledger_corruption  [B]
      An evidence-quad ledger_hash is tampered.
      Required property: clean slice PASSES; mutated slice DETECTED (verifier exits non-zero)
      Recovery: verifier flags the break; the append-only chain is not advanced past the
      corrupted record (no downstream actuation on a broken chain).
    partial_ledger_loss  [B]
      A decision record is lost from the chain.
      Required property: clean slice PASSES; mutated slice DETECTED (verifier exits non-zero)
      Recovery: verifier flags the break; the append-only chain is not advanced past the
      corrupted record (no downstream actuation on a broken chain).
    event_reordering  [B]
      Two decision events are reordered.
      Required property: clean slice PASSES; mutated slice DETECTED (verifier exits non-zero)
      Recovery: verifier flags the break; the append-only chain is not advanced past the
